{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistencecoordinator\/mergeremote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Re-hydration restricted to the rows a caller already knows changed."}],"metadata":{"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeRemote"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Store","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ids"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Set","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"deleted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Set","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"policy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MergePolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"title":"mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","extendedModule":"SwiduxPersistence","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0B11CoordinatorCAA0A00A10ObservableRzrlE11mergeRemote4into3ids7deleted6policyyAD5StoreCyxq_G_Shy10Foundation4UUIDVGAqA11MergePolicyVSgtYaF","symbolKind":"method"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeRemote"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"store"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","text":"Store"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ids"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"deleted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID"},{"kind":"text","text":"> = [], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"policy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","text":"MergePolicy"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"store","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The live store to reconcile.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"ids","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The identities to re-read. IDs matching no row, and IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"belonging to another entity type, are harmless."}]}]},{"name":"deleted","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Identities known to have been deleted elsewhere.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"policy","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Narrows the configured policy for this call only."}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The O(k) counterpart to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which re-reads every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row of every registered entity on every tick. Where a sync signal carries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"text":" identities changed, this spends that knowledge: one batched fetch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per 500 IDs instead of a full-table scan, and only the named entities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconciled. Everything else in state is left exactly as it was.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every guarantee ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes holds here. Pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes are flushed first; an ID with unflushed local intent — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drained-but-unflushed write, an un-drained edit, a pending deletion, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"write whose save failed, or an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing"},{"text":" hold — always wins, and that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not configurable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A partial read cannot tell a deleted row from one that was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never asked about, so this ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"never","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" infers a deletion. An ID vanishes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only if you name it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleted"},{"type":"text","text":", and only if the resolved policy grants"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/removesMissingEntities"},{"type":"text","text":". Name only what you have positive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"evidence for — a history tombstone, not an empty fetch. In exchange,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there is no empty-snapshot guard to work around: this can remove the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last surviving entity, which ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" cannot.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ID named in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleted"},{"text":" that storage ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"still holds"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" is not removed. A live"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row is evidence the deletion was itself undone elsewhere; a tombstone can","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be stale."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Deferred rows are re-offered","level":2,"anchor":"Deferred-rows-are-re-offered"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tick may read a row and decline to apply it — an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing"},{"type":"text","text":" hold is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exemption that leaves no other trace. Those rows are remembered by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity and re-offered on the next call, on top of whatever "},{"code":"ids","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" names,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a caller does not have to re-queue them against its own signal. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matters here because a sync signal is generally not resent and releasing a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hold writes no transaction of its own, so without it a hold would quietly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"become a veto. A call whose read throws is remembered the same way: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identities it was handed are owed, not dropped with the read."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeChanges(into:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" shares the same debt, so"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"either path settles what the other deferred. Both discard it when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"container is swapped.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Registered "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse:"},{"type":"text","text":" resolvers do not run here — a resolver is handed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the whole table and asked which rows survive, and a subset would have it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"judge a world it cannot see. Duplicate rows are still collapsed on read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and still reported. Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/collapseDuplicates(into:)-7d2no"},{"type":"text","text":" or a full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to reclaim them."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistenceCoordinator/rehydrate(into:policy:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rehydrate"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Store"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"